## 3. Important Code Deep Dive

### 3.1 Optimistic Locking via Atomic Conditional Updates (`submission.service.ts`)
```typescript
// Atomically transition from QUEUED -> RUNNING.
// updateMany translates to: UPDATE submissions SET status = 'RUNNING' WHERE id = $1 AND status = 'QUEUED'
const transitionToRunning = await prisma.submission.updateMany({
  where: {
    id: submissionId,
    status: SubmissionStatus.QUEUED, // Guard: MUST be currently QUEUED
  },
  data: { status: SubmissionStatus.RUNNING },
});

if (transitionToRunning.count === 0) {
  logger.warn(
    { submissionId },
    'Optimistic locking aborted: Submission is no longer in QUEUED state (already claimed or processed)'
  );
  return; // Safely abort without spawning redundant Docker containers
}
```
**Why this is interview gold:**
Under high concurrency, PostgreSQL locks the row during the `UPDATE`. If Worker A and Worker B run this concurrently, exactly one will update 1 row (`count: 1`), while the other updates 0 rows (`count: 0`) and safely bails out. No distributed locks or Redis mutexes required!

### 3.2 Terminal State Immutability Guard (`submission.service.ts`)
```typescript
const finalizeResult = await prisma.submission.updateMany({
  where: {
    id: submissionId,
    status: SubmissionStatus.RUNNING, // Guard: MUST be currently RUNNING
  },
  data: {
    status: result.status,
    executionTimeMs: result.executionTimeMs,
    memoryUsedMb: result.memoryUsedMb,
    errorOutput: result.errorOutput,
    failedTestCaseIndex: result.failedTestCaseIndex,
  },
});

if (finalizeResult.count === 0) {
  logger.warn('Terminal update aborted: Submission was already finalized');
  return;
}
```
Once a submission enters `ACCEPTED`, `WRONG_ANSWER`, or `TIME_LIMIT_EXCEEDED`, its status in PostgreSQL is no longer `RUNNING`. Any delayed or rogue process attempting to finalize the record will see `count === 0` and be rejected.

### 3.3 Dead-Letter Queue (DLQ) Quarantine (`submissionConsumer.ts`)
```typescript
worker.on('failed', async (job, err) => {
  const maxAttempts = job.opts.attempts ?? 1;
  const isExhausted = job.attemptsMade >= maxAttempts;

  if (isExhausted) {
    // 1. Quarantine to DLQ for engineer inspection
    await sendToDeadLetterQueue({
      submissionId: job.data.submissionId,
      originalJobId: job.id,
      failedReason: err.message,
      attemptsMade: job.attemptsMade,
      failedAt: new Date().toISOString(),
      stack: err.stack,
    });

    // 2. Mark submission in PostgreSQL as SYSTEM_ERROR so user isn't stuck on RUNNING
    await prisma.submission.updateMany({
      where: {
        id: job.data.submissionId,
        status: { in: [SubmissionStatus.QUEUED, SubmissionStatus.RUNNING] },
      },
      data: {
        status: SubmissionStatus.SYSTEM_ERROR,
        errorOutput: `System Error: Evaluation failed after ${job.attemptsMade} attempts due to infrastructure error.`,
      },
    });
  }
});
```

